# Rat cradle, cut at z = -80 ... +80 mm, in polyethylene.
# The shape comes from the 511 keV attenuation map (mu-map) of the Quad86 coil with the rat cradle: I turned
# the cradle into STL surfaces and import them as tessellated volumes, 10 parts in real size, notches
# included (stl/ and stl80/). Axial details shorter than 2 mm were averaged.
# Material: Bed_HDPE (polyethylene C2H4, 0.95 g/cm3, defined in Coil3Bed.db), the same as the mouse cradle.
# It is an assumption: the real cradles are white and opaque, probably polyethylene. I do not use the
# value of the map (mu 0.0744 /cm at 511 keV, 0.80 g/cm3 as C5H8O2), because it is lower than that of any
# solid plastic. The STL file names carry the label of that map value (Plastic_0744).
# The wall thicknesses agree with my caliper measurements.
# Every part is placed at (0, {cradleY}, {sourceZ}); both aliases are set in the main macro, so the cradle
# moves with the source along z. Every part attaches its own PhantomSD.

/gate/world/daughters/name ratbed_s0087
/gate/world/daughters/insert tessellated
/gate/ratbed_s0087/geometry/setPathToSTLFile coil_bed_real/stl80/bed_s0087_Plastic_0744.stl
/gate/ratbed_s0087/setMaterial Bed_HDPE
/gate/ratbed_s0087/placement/setTranslation 0 {cradleY} {sourceZ} mm
/gate/ratbed_s0087/vis/setColor white
/gate/ratbed_s0087/attachPhantomSD

/gate/world/daughters/name ratbed_s0088
/gate/world/daughters/insert tessellated
/gate/ratbed_s0088/geometry/setPathToSTLFile coil_bed_real/stl/bed_s0088_Plastic_0744.stl
/gate/ratbed_s0088/setMaterial Bed_HDPE
/gate/ratbed_s0088/placement/setTranslation 0 {cradleY} {sourceZ} mm
/gate/ratbed_s0088/vis/setColor white
/gate/ratbed_s0088/attachPhantomSD

